From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 04:36:28 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] startupfeedback: The launch feedback follows the pointer
 in depth

The busy cursor drew its icon in paintScreen, after the scene, with no
parallax, so over a window beneath the active one it stayed at the screen's
depth while the pointer was drawn at that window's level. On an output that
shows stereo depth the icon is now part of the pointer: it takes the pointer's
plane through the same eased motion, and the bounce goes in depth only, from
the pointer's plane up to the popped limit of the output above it (the icon
keeps its place on the screen); the blinking and static feedback take the
plane. On an output that does not show 3D the bounce is KDE's own, and the
effect follows the output under the pointer. A frame property holds the
animation for tests.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 via Claude Code
---
 .../startupfeedback/startupfeedback.cpp       | 79 ++++++++++++++++---
 src/plugins/startupfeedback/startupfeedback.h | 19 +++++
 2 files changed, 89 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

